window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b249-8bbd5e00b7326c8d.json"]={sha256:"8bbd5e00b7326c8dd9c50e975bf64c1db15affd244d9f9f8bf36da2b813c0e56",value:{"id":"b249","title":"溢洪道氣蝕防治","titleEn":"Cavitation mitigation in spillways","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以由絕對壓力缺陷含氣與修補驗證氣蝕防治為主線，先用絕對壓力與蒸氣壓與氣蝕指標與速度界定水力與構造條件，再將摻氣量與相分率、拋離空腔與再附著連結到運轉曝露與追蹤。氣蝕指標與含氣算例只作機制比較，起蝕門檻依表面幾何水質與流況而變。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops verifying cavitation mitigation through absolute pressure defects aeration and repair through Absolute pressure and vapor pressure and Cavitation index and velocity, then connects Air supply and phase fraction and Jet cavity and reattachment to Operating exposure and follow-up. Cavitation indices and aeration examples compare mechanisms; inception thresholds depend on surface geometry water quality and flow conditions. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["絕對壓力與蒸氣壓","Absolute pressure and vapor pressure"],["錯台尺度與流動分離","Offset scale and separation"],["摻氣量與相分率","Air supply and phase fraction"],["拋離空腔與再附著","Jet cavity and reattachment"],["運轉曝露與追蹤","Operating exposure and follow-up"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["絕對壓力與蒸氣壓","錯台尺度與流動分離","摻氣量與相分率","拋離空腔與再附著","運轉曝露與追蹤"],"labelsEn":["Absolute pressure and vapor pressure","Offset scale and separation","Air supply and phase fraction","Jet cavity and reattachment","Operating exposure and follow-up"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查絕對壓力與蒸氣壓：atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa；再獨立檢查氣蝕指標與速度：pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885。敏感度：絕對壓力100kPa與蒸氣壓2.3kPa不變，速度由20增至30m/s，氣蝕指標由0.4885降至0.2171；速度增加50%使動壓增加125%，但不能由指標直接預報破壞速率。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。氣蝕指標與含氣算例只作機制比較，起蝕門檻依表面幾何水質與流況而變。 將用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Absolute pressure and vapor pressure: atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa. Independently examine Cavitation index and velocity: pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885. Sensitivity: holding absolute pressure at100kPa and vapor pressure at2.3kPa, increasing speed from20 to30m/s lowers the index from0.4885 to0.2171. Dynamic pressure increases125 percent, but the index alone does not predict damage rate. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Cavitation indices and aeration examples compare mechanisms; inception thresholds depend on surface geometry water quality and flow conditions. Use the following independent check: Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b249-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」與「氣蝕指標與速度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Absolute pressure and vapor pressure\" and \"Cavitation index and velocity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b249-v15-01","title":"絕對壓力與蒸氣壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」如何影響溢洪道氣蝕防治的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Absolute pressure and vapor pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cavitation mitigation in spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"氣蝕涉及局部壓力接近液體蒸氣壓，兩者必須使用相同絕對壓力基準。高程與天氣會改變大氣壓，水溫則改變蒸氣壓；把表壓直接相減會嚴重錯估餘量。量測時須記錄壓力校正與溫度，而非只報單一負壓數值。 驗證時應將氣壓計與壓力感測器零點校正對齊並記錄水溫，並辨識以下失效情境：混用表壓與絕對壓會錯估距離氣化條件的餘量。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cavitation concerns local pressure approaching vapor pressure, both on an absolute basis. Altitude and weather affect atmospheric pressure while temperature affects vapor pressure. Subtracting gauge pressure directly gives the wrong margin; record pressure calibration and temperature instead of reporting only one negative gauge value. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Align barometer and pressure-sensor zero checks and record water temperature. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Mixing gauge and absolute pressure misstates the margin to vapor formation. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Absolute pressure and vapor pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「表壓負值就表示液體一定已達蒸氣壓」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any negative gauge pressure proves that liquid has reached vapor pressure\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Absolute pressure and vapor pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-01-k1","title":"絕對壓力與蒸氣壓","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor pressure","text":"氣蝕涉及局部壓力接近液體蒸氣壓，兩者必須使用相同絕對壓力基準。高程與天氣會改變大氣壓，水溫則改變蒸氣壓；把表壓直接相減會嚴重錯估餘量。","textEn":"Cavitation concerns local pressure approaching vapor pressure, both on an absolute basis. Altitude and weather affect atmospheric pressure while temperature affects vapor pressure.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：表壓負值就表示液體一定已達蒸氣壓 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any negative gauge pressure proves that liquid has reached vapor pressure Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Absolute pressure and vapor pressure\" is correct?","options":["表壓負值就表示液體一定已達蒸氣壓","氣蝕涉及局部壓力接近液體蒸氣壓，兩者必須使用相同絕對壓力基準。","氣蝕指標數值可直接換算成混凝土磨損速率"],"optionsEn":["Any negative gauge pressure proves that liquid has reached vapor pressure","Cavitation concerns local pressure approaching vapor pressure, both on an absolute basis.","The cavitation index directly converts into a concrete damage rate"],"answer":1,"explanation":"氣蝕涉及局部壓力接近液體蒸氣壓，兩者必須使用相同絕對壓力基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cavitation concerns local pressure approaching vapor pressure, both on an absolute basis. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b249-v15-02","title":"絕對壓力與蒸氣壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Absolute pressure and vapor pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將氣壓計與壓力感測器零點校正對齊並記錄水溫。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align barometer and pressure-sensor zero checks and record water temperature.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Absolute pressure and vapor pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["平均壓力高於蒸氣壓就排除所有瞬間氣蝕","空腔越負壓就表示摻氣保護一定越好","原創教學假設：atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa。"],"optionsEn":["Mean pressure above vapor pressure excludes every transient cavitation event","Stronger cavity suction always means better aeration protection","Original teaching assumptions: atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: atmosphericPressure=90 kPa; gaugePressure=-35 kPa; absolutePressure=90-35=55 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b249-v15-03","title":"絕對壓力與蒸氣壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Absolute pressure and vapor pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將氣壓計與壓力感測器零點校正對齊並記錄水溫。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「混用表壓與絕對壓會錯估距離氣化條件的餘量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align barometer and pressure-sensor zero checks and record water temperature. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Mixing gauge and absolute pressure misstates the margin to vapor formation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以將氣壓計與壓力感測器零點校正對齊並記錄水溫作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對混用表壓與絕對壓會錯估距離氣化條件的餘量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Align barometer and pressure-sensor zero checks and record water temperature. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Mixing gauge and absolute pressure misstates the margin to vapor formation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：混用表壓與絕對壓會錯估距離氣化條件的餘量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing gauge and absolute pressure misstates the margin to vapor formation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將氣壓計與壓力感測器零點校正對齊並記錄水溫。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「混用表壓與絕對壓會錯估距離氣化條件的餘量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Align barometer and pressure-sensor zero checks and record water temperature. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Mixing gauge and absolute pressure misstates the margin to vapor formation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以將氣壓計與壓力感測器零點校正對齊並記錄水溫作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對混用表壓與絕對壓會錯估距離氣化條件的餘量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Align barometer and pressure-sensor zero checks and record water temperature. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Mixing gauge and absolute pressure misstates the margin to vapor formation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Absolute pressure and vapor pressure\"?","options":["將氣壓計與壓力感測器零點校正對齊並記錄水溫。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","一次損傷體積可直接預報未來每年的固定損失"],"optionsEn":["Align barometer and pressure-sensor zero checks and record water temperature.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","One damage-volume survey predicts a fixed annual future loss"],"answer":0,"explanation":"將氣壓計與壓力感測器零點校正對齊並記錄水溫。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align barometer and pressure-sensor zero checks and record water temperature. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b249-v15-04","title":"絕對壓力與蒸氣壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Absolute pressure and vapor pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"混用表壓與絕對壓會錯估距離氣化條件的餘量。診斷時應採取以下查核：將氣壓計與壓力感測器零點校正對齊並記錄水溫，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing gauge and absolute pressure misstates the margin to vapor formation. Diagnose it by the following check: Align barometer and pressure-sensor zero checks and record water temperature. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「表壓負值就表示液體一定已達蒸氣壓」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any negative gauge pressure proves that liquid has reached vapor pressure\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"混用表壓與絕對壓會錯估距離氣化條件的餘量。診斷時應採取以下查核：將氣壓計與壓力感測器零點校正對齊並記錄水溫，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Mixing gauge and absolute pressure misstates the margin to vapor formation. Diagnose it by the following check: Align barometer and pressure-sensor zero checks and record water temperature. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「絕對壓力與蒸氣壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Absolute pressure and vapor pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","混用表壓與絕對壓會錯估距離氣化條件的餘量。","氣蝕指標數值可直接換算成混凝土磨損速率"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Mixing gauge and absolute pressure misstates the margin to vapor formation.","The cavitation index directly converts into a concrete damage rate"],"answer":1,"explanation":"混用表壓與絕對壓會錯估距離氣化條件的餘量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing gauge and absolute pressure misstates the margin to vapor formation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b249-v15-05","title":"氣蝕指標與速度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cavitation index and velocity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「氣蝕指標與速度」如何影響溢洪道氣蝕防治的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cavitation index and velocity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cavitation mitigation in spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"氣蝕指標把高於蒸氣壓的壓力餘量除以參考動壓，可比較局部低壓對高速水流的相對程度。分母速度必須與起蝕資料使用相同定義；指標不是破壞速率，表面不平整、氣核與含氣保護仍會改變實際結果。 驗證時應同步量測參考速度與局部壓力並標明指標定義，並辨識以下失效情境：採不同位置速度比較門檻會造成不一致判讀。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「氣蝕指標與速度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The cavitation index normalizes pressure margin above vapor pressure by a reference dynamic pressure. Its velocity definition must match the inception data used for comparison. The index is not a damage-rate law; surface irregularities, nuclei and protective aeration still affect the physical outcome. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure reference velocity and local pressure together and state the index definition. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using velocities from different reference locations makes threshold comparisons inconsistent. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cavitation index and velocity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885.","failure":"常見誤解：「氣蝕指標數值可直接換算成混凝土磨損速率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The cavitation index directly converts into a concrete damage rate\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「氣蝕指標與速度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cavitation index and velocity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-05-k1","title":"氣蝕指標與速度","titleEn":"Cavitation index and velocity","text":"氣蝕指標把高於蒸氣壓的壓力餘量除以參考動壓，可比較局部低壓對高速水流的相對程度。分母速度必須與起蝕資料使用相同定義；指標不是破壞速率，表面不平整、氣核與含氣保護仍會改變實際結果。","textEn":"The cavitation index normalizes pressure margin above vapor pressure by a reference dynamic pressure. Its velocity definition must match the inception data used for comparison.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：氣蝕指標數值可直接換算成混凝土磨損速率 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The cavitation index directly converts into a concrete damage rate Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氣蝕指標與速度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cavitation index and velocity\" is correct?","options":["氣蝕指標數值可直接換算成混凝土磨損速率","相同錯台高度不論方向都有相同氣蝕影響","氣蝕指標把高於蒸氣壓的壓力餘量除以參考動壓，可比較局部低壓對高速水流的相對程度。"],"optionsEn":["The cavitation index directly converts into a concrete damage rate","Equal offset heights have identical cavitation effects in every orientation","The cavitation index normalizes pressure margin above vapor pressure by a reference dynamic pressure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"氣蝕指標把高於蒸氣壓的壓力餘量除以參考動壓，可比較局部低壓對高速水流的相對程度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The cavitation index normalizes pressure margin above vapor pressure by a reference dynamic pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b249-v15-06","title":"氣蝕指標與速度：定量估算","titleEn":"Cavitation index and velocity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「氣蝕指標與速度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cavitation index and velocity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測參考速度與局部壓力並標明指標定義。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure reference velocity and local pressure together and state the index definition.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「氣蝕指標與速度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cavitation index and velocity\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885。","總供氣量足夠就保證每個壁面都有足夠含氣","只要有摻氣坎就不可能發生空腔淹沒"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885.","Adequate total air supply guarantees adequate aeration at every wall","The presence of an aerator ramp makes cavity drowning impossible"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pAbsolute=100 kPa; pVapor=2.3 kPa; rho=1000 kg/m3; V=20 m/s; sigma=(100000-2300)/(0.5*1000*20**2)=0.4885. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b249-v15-07","title":"氣蝕指標與速度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cavitation index and velocity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「氣蝕指標與速度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cavitation index and velocity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測參考速度與局部壓力並標明指標定義。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「採不同位置速度比較門檻會造成不一致判讀」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure reference velocity and local pressure together and state the index definition. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using velocities from different reference locations makes threshold comparisons inconsistent. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步量測參考速度與局部壓力並標明指標定義作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對採不同位置速度比較門檻會造成不一致判讀，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure reference velocity and local pressure together and state the index definition. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using velocities from different reference locations makes threshold comparisons inconsistent. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：採不同位置速度比較門檻會造成不一致判讀。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using velocities from different reference locations makes threshold comparisons inconsistent. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測參考速度與局部壓力並標明指標定義。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「採不同位置速度比較門檻會造成不一致判讀」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure reference velocity and local pressure together and state the index definition. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using velocities from different reference locations makes threshold comparisons inconsistent. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步量測參考速度與局部壓力並標明指標定義作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對採不同位置速度比較門檻會造成不一致判讀，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure reference velocity and local pressure together and state the index definition. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using velocities from different reference locations makes threshold comparisons inconsistent. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「氣蝕指標與速度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cavitation index and velocity\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","同步量測參考速度與局部壓力並標明指標定義。","一個拉拔試點合格就證明整片修補完全黏結"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure reference velocity and local pressure together and state the index definition.","One passing pull-off test proves complete bond over the entire repair"],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步量測參考速度與局部壓力並標明指標定義。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure reference velocity and local pressure together and state the index definition. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b249-v15-08","title":"氣蝕指標與速度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cavitation index and velocity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「氣蝕指標與速度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cavitation index and velocity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"採不同位置速度比較門檻會造成不一致判讀。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測參考速度與局部壓力並標明指標定義，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using velocities from different reference locations makes threshold comparisons inconsistent. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure reference velocity and local pressure together and state the index definition. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「氣蝕指標數值可直接換算成混凝土磨損速率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The cavitation index directly converts into a concrete damage rate\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"採不同位置速度比較門檻會造成不一致判讀。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測參考速度與局部壓力並標明指標定義，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Using velocities from different reference locations makes threshold comparisons inconsistent. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure reference velocity and local pressure together and state the index definition. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「氣蝕指標與速度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cavitation index and velocity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","相同錯台高度不論方向都有相同氣蝕影響","採不同位置速度比較門檻會造成不一致判讀。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal offset heights have identical cavitation effects in every orientation","Using velocities from different reference locations makes threshold comparisons inconsistent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"採不同位置速度比較門檻會造成不一致判讀。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using velocities from different reference locations makes threshold comparisons inconsistent. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b249-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「錯台尺度與流動分離」與「低壓脈動與極值」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Offset scale and separation\" and \"Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b249-v15-09","title":"錯台尺度與流動分離：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Offset scale and separation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「錯台尺度與流動分離」如何影響溢洪道氣蝕防治的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Offset scale and separation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cavitation mitigation in spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"迎流錯台使水流突然偏轉，背後低壓與渦流可能觸發氣蝕；缺陷方向和尖銳程度比單純高度更重要。相對粗糙度可描述尺度但不能提供通用允收值，施工驗收須保留沿流方向的剖面及表面修整紀錄。 驗證時應用沿流剖面儀量測錯台方向高度與前後坡度，並辨識以下失效情境：只量垂直高度會漏掉尖銳迎流邊緣的分離效應。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「錯台尺度與流動分離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An upstream-facing offset abruptly deflects flow and creates low pressure and vortices behind it. Orientation and sharpness matter alongside height. Relative roughness describes scale but is not a universal tolerance; acceptance needs profiles along the flow direction and documented surface finishing. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Profile the surface along flow to measure offset direction, height and adjoining slopes. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Measuring height alone misses separation at a sharp upstream-facing edge. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Offset scale and separation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：offsetHeight=0.004 m; localFlowDepth=0.80 m; relativeOffset=0.004/0.80=0.005 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: offsetHeight=0.004 m; localFlowDepth=0.80 m; relativeOffset=0.004/0.80=0.005 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「相同錯台高度不論方向都有相同氣蝕影響」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal offset heights have identical cavitation effects in every orientation\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「錯台尺度與流動分離」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Offset scale and separation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-09-k1","title":"錯台尺度與流動分離","titleEn":"Offset scale and separation","text":"迎流錯台使水流突然偏轉，背後低壓與渦流可能觸發氣蝕；缺陷方向和尖銳程度比單純高度更重要。相對粗糙度可描述尺度但不能提供通用允收值，施工驗收須保留沿流方向的剖面及表面修整紀錄。","textEn":"An upstream-facing offset abruptly deflects flow and creates low pressure and vortices behind it. Orientation and sharpness matter alongside height.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相同錯台高度不論方向都有相同氣蝕影響 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal offset heights have identical cavitation effects in every orientation Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「錯台尺度與流動分離」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Offset scale and separation\" is correct?","options":["迎流錯台使水流突然偏轉，背後低壓與渦流可能觸發氣蝕；缺陷方向和尖銳程度比單純高度更重要。","相同錯台高度不論方向都有相同氣蝕影響","平均壓力高於蒸氣壓就排除所有瞬間氣蝕"],"optionsEn":["An upstream-facing offset abruptly deflects flow and creates low pressure and vortices behind it.","Equal offset heights have identical cavitation effects in every orientation","Mean pressure above vapor pressure excludes every transient cavitation event"],"answer":0,"explanation":"迎流錯台使水流突然偏轉，背後低壓與渦流可能觸發氣蝕；缺陷方向和尖銳程度比單純高度更重要。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An upstream-facing offset abruptly deflects flow and creates low pressure and vortices behind it. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b249-v15-10","title":"錯台尺度與流動分離：定量估算","titleEn":"Offset scale and separation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「錯台尺度與流動分離」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Offset scale and separation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：offsetHeight=0.004 m; localFlowDepth=0.80 m; relativeOffset=0.004/0.80=0.005 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: offsetHeight=0.004 m; localFlowDepth=0.80 m; relativeOffset=0.004/0.80=0.005 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用沿流剖面儀量測錯台方向高度與前後坡度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Profile the surface along flow to measure offset direction, height and adjoining slopes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：offsetHeight=0.004 m; localFlowDepth=0.80 m; relativeOffset=0.004/0.80=0.005 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: offsetHeight=0.004 m; localFlowDepth=0.80 m; relativeOffset=0.004/0.80=0.005 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「錯台尺度與流動分離」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Offset scale and separation\", which statement holds?","options":["空腔越負壓就表示摻氣保護一定越好","原創教學假設：offsetHeight=0.004 m; localFlowDepth=0.80 m; relativeOffset=0.004/0.80=0.005 dimensionless。","一次損傷體積可直接預報未來每年的固定損失"],"optionsEn":["Stronger cavity suction always means better aeration protection","Original teaching assumptions: offsetHeight=0.004 m; localFlowDepth=0.80 m; relativeOffset=0.004/0.80=0.005 dimensionless.","One damage-volume survey predicts a fixed annual future loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：offsetHeight=0.004 m; localFlowDepth=0.80 m; relativeOffset=0.004/0.80=0.005 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: offsetHeight=0.004 m; localFlowDepth=0.80 m; relativeOffset=0.004/0.80=0.005 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b249-v15-11","title":"錯台尺度與流動分離：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Offset scale and separation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「錯台尺度與流動分離」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Offset scale and separation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用沿流剖面儀量測錯台方向高度與前後坡度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只量垂直高度會漏掉尖銳迎流邊緣的分離效應」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Profile the surface along flow to measure offset direction, height and adjoining slopes. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Measuring height alone misses separation at a sharp upstream-facing edge. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以用沿流剖面儀量測錯台方向高度與前後坡度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只量垂直高度會漏掉尖銳迎流邊緣的分離效應，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Profile the surface along flow to measure offset direction, height and adjoining slopes. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Measuring height alone misses separation at a sharp upstream-facing edge. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只量垂直高度會漏掉尖銳迎流邊緣的分離效應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Measuring height alone misses separation at a sharp upstream-facing edge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用沿流剖面儀量測錯台方向高度與前後坡度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只量垂直高度會漏掉尖銳迎流邊緣的分離效應」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Profile the surface along flow to measure offset direction, height and adjoining slopes. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Measuring height alone misses separation at a sharp upstream-facing edge. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以用沿流剖面儀量測錯台方向高度與前後坡度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只量垂直高度會漏掉尖銳迎流邊緣的分離效應，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Profile the surface along flow to measure offset direction, height and adjoining slopes. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Measuring height alone misses separation at a sharp upstream-facing edge. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「錯台尺度與流動分離」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Offset scale and separation\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","所有運轉一小時造成的氣蝕損傷必定相同","用沿流剖面儀量測錯台方向高度與前後坡度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Every operating hour necessarily causes the same cavitation damage","Profile the surface along flow to measure offset direction, height and adjoining slopes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用沿流剖面儀量測錯台方向高度與前後坡度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Profile the surface along flow to measure offset direction, height and adjoining slopes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b249-v15-12","title":"錯台尺度與流動分離：失效診斷","titleEn":"Offset scale and separation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「錯台尺度與流動分離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Offset scale and separation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只量垂直高度會漏掉尖銳迎流邊緣的分離效應。診斷時應採取以下查核：用沿流剖面儀量測錯台方向高度與前後坡度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Measuring height alone misses separation at a sharp upstream-facing edge. Diagnose it by the following check: Profile the surface along flow to measure offset direction, height and adjoining slopes. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相同錯台高度不論方向都有相同氣蝕影響」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal offset heights have identical cavitation effects in every orientation\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只量垂直高度會漏掉尖銳迎流邊緣的分離效應。診斷時應採取以下查核：用沿流剖面儀量測錯台方向高度與前後坡度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Measuring height alone misses separation at a sharp upstream-facing edge. Diagnose it by the following check: Profile the surface along flow to measure offset direction, height and adjoining slopes. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「錯台尺度與流動分離」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Offset scale and separation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只量垂直高度會漏掉尖銳迎流邊緣的分離效應。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","平均壓力高於蒸氣壓就排除所有瞬間氣蝕"],"optionsEn":["Measuring height alone misses separation at a sharp upstream-facing edge.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Mean pressure above vapor pressure excludes every transient cavitation event"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只量垂直高度會漏掉尖銳迎流邊緣的分離效應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Measuring height alone misses separation at a sharp upstream-facing edge. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b249-v15-13","title":"低壓脈動與極值：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「低壓脈動與極值」如何影響溢洪道氣蝕防治的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cavitation mitigation in spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平均壓力高於蒸氣壓不表示所有瞬間都安全，紊流脈動可能產生短暫低壓。高斯近似可示範統計尾部但未必適用實際尖峰；應保存原始高頻資料並分析持續時間、空間相關與感測器頻率響應，避免只用平均值判讀。 驗證時應檢查低壓事件的持續時間與相鄰測點是否同步，並辨識以下失效情境：將均值減三倍標準差當絕對下限會漏掉非高斯尖峰。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「低壓脈動與極值」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A mean above vapor pressure does not exclude brief low-pressure excursions. A Gaussian illustration describes a statistical tail but may not fit actual spikes. Preserve high-rate records and analyze duration, spatial correlation and sensor response rather than judging the condition from the average alone. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Examine excursion duration and synchronization between neighboring pressure sensors. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Treating mean minus three deviations as a hard minimum misses non-Gaussian spikes. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Illustrative meanAbsolutePressure=70 kPa; standardDeviation=15 kPa; meanMinus3SD=70-3*15=25 kPa; no physical minimum implied。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative meanAbsolutePressure=70 kPa; standardDeviation=15 kPa; meanMinus3SD=70-3*15=25 kPa; no physical minimum implied.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均壓力高於蒸氣壓就排除所有瞬間氣蝕」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Mean pressure above vapor pressure excludes every transient cavitation event\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「低壓脈動與極值」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-13-k1","title":"低壓脈動與極值","titleEn":"Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes","text":"平均壓力高於蒸氣壓不表示所有瞬間都安全，紊流脈動可能產生短暫低壓。高斯近似可示範統計尾部但未必適用實際尖峰；應保存原始高頻資料並分析持續時間、空間相關與感測器頻率響應，避免只用平均值判讀。","textEn":"A mean above vapor pressure does not exclude brief low-pressure excursions. A Gaussian illustration describes a statistical tail but may not fit actual spikes.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均壓力高於蒸氣壓就排除所有瞬間氣蝕 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Mean pressure above vapor pressure excludes every transient cavitation event Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「低壓脈動與極值」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes\" is correct?","options":["平均壓力高於蒸氣壓就排除所有瞬間氣蝕","平均壓力高於蒸氣壓不表示所有瞬間都安全，紊流脈動可能產生短暫低壓。","總供氣量足夠就保證每個壁面都有足夠含氣"],"optionsEn":["Mean pressure above vapor pressure excludes every transient cavitation event","A mean above vapor pressure does not exclude brief low-pressure excursions.","Adequate total air supply guarantees adequate aeration at every wall"],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均壓力高於蒸氣壓不表示所有瞬間都安全，紊流脈動可能產生短暫低壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A mean above vapor pressure does not exclude brief low-pressure excursions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b249-v15-14","title":"低壓脈動與極值：定量估算","titleEn":"Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「低壓脈動與極值」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Illustrative meanAbsolutePressure=70 kPa; standardDeviation=15 kPa; meanMinus3SD=70-3*15=25 kPa; no physical minimum implied。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative meanAbsolutePressure=70 kPa; standardDeviation=15 kPa; meanMinus3SD=70-3*15=25 kPa; no physical minimum implied. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：檢查低壓事件的持續時間與相鄰測點是否同步。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Examine excursion duration and synchronization between neighboring pressure sensors.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Illustrative meanAbsolutePressure=70 kPa; standardDeviation=15 kPa; meanMinus3SD=70-3*15=25 kPa; no physical minimum implied。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative meanAbsolutePressure=70 kPa; standardDeviation=15 kPa; meanMinus3SD=70-3*15=25 kPa; no physical minimum implied. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「低壓脈動與極值」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes\", which statement holds?","options":["只要有摻氣坎就不可能發生空腔淹沒","一個拉拔試點合格就證明整片修補完全黏結","原創教學假設：Illustrative meanAbsolutePressure=70 kPa; standardDeviation=15 kPa; meanMinus3SD=70-3*15=25 kPa; no physical minimum implied。"],"optionsEn":["The presence of an aerator ramp makes cavity drowning impossible","One passing pull-off test proves complete bond over the entire repair","Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative meanAbsolutePressure=70 kPa; standardDeviation=15 kPa; meanMinus3SD=70-3*15=25 kPa; no physical minimum implied."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Illustrative meanAbsolutePressure=70 kPa; standardDeviation=15 kPa; meanMinus3SD=70-3*15=25 kPa; no physical minimum implied。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative meanAbsolutePressure=70 kPa; standardDeviation=15 kPa; meanMinus3SD=70-3*15=25 kPa; no physical minimum implied. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b249-v15-15","title":"低壓脈動與極值：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「低壓脈動與極值」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"檢查低壓事件的持續時間與相鄰測點是否同步。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「將均值減三倍標準差當絕對下限會漏掉非高斯尖峰」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Examine excursion duration and synchronization between neighboring pressure sensors. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating mean minus three deviations as a hard minimum misses non-Gaussian spikes. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以檢查低壓事件的持續時間與相鄰測點是否同步作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對將均值減三倍標準差當絕對下限會漏掉非高斯尖峰，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Examine excursion duration and synchronization between neighboring pressure sensors. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating mean minus three deviations as a hard minimum misses non-Gaussian spikes. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：將均值減三倍標準差當絕對下限會漏掉非高斯尖峰。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating mean minus three deviations as a hard minimum misses non-Gaussian spikes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"檢查低壓事件的持續時間與相鄰測點是否同步。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「將均值減三倍標準差當絕對下限會漏掉非高斯尖峰」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Examine excursion duration and synchronization between neighboring pressure sensors. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating mean minus three deviations as a hard minimum misses non-Gaussian spikes. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以檢查低壓事件的持續時間與相鄰測點是否同步作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對將均值減三倍標準差當絕對下限會漏掉非高斯尖峰，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Examine excursion duration and synchronization between neighboring pressure sensors. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating mean minus three deviations as a hard minimum misses non-Gaussian spikes. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「低壓脈動與極值」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes\"?","options":["檢查低壓事件的持續時間與相鄰測點是否同步。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","表壓負值就表示液體一定已達蒸氣壓"],"optionsEn":["Examine excursion duration and synchronization between neighboring pressure sensors.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Any negative gauge pressure proves that liquid has reached vapor pressure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"檢查低壓事件的持續時間與相鄰測點是否同步。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Examine excursion duration and synchronization between neighboring pressure sensors. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b249-v15-16","title":"低壓脈動與極值：失效診斷","titleEn":"Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「低壓脈動與極值」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將均值減三倍標準差當絕對下限會漏掉非高斯尖峰。診斷時應採取以下查核：檢查低壓事件的持續時間與相鄰測點是否同步，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating mean minus three deviations as a hard minimum misses non-Gaussian spikes. Diagnose it by the following check: Examine excursion duration and synchronization between neighboring pressure sensors. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均壓力高於蒸氣壓就排除所有瞬間氣蝕」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Mean pressure above vapor pressure excludes every transient cavitation event\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將均值減三倍標準差當絕對下限會漏掉非高斯尖峰。診斷時應採取以下查核：檢查低壓事件的持續時間與相鄰測點是否同步，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Treating mean minus three deviations as a hard minimum misses non-Gaussian spikes. Diagnose it by the following check: Examine excursion duration and synchronization between neighboring pressure sensors. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「低壓脈動與極值」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Low-pressure fluctuations and extremes\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","將均值減三倍標準差當絕對下限會漏掉非高斯尖峰。","總供氣量足夠就保證每個壁面都有足夠含氣"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating mean minus three deviations as a hard minimum misses non-Gaussian spikes.","Adequate total air supply guarantees adequate aeration at every wall"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將均值減三倍標準差當絕對下限會漏掉非高斯尖峰。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating mean minus three deviations as a hard minimum misses non-Gaussian spikes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b249-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「摻氣量與相分率」與「通氣管損失與負壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Air supply and phase fraction\" and \"Vent losses and suction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b249-v15-17","title":"摻氣量與相分率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Air supply and phase fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「摻氣量與相分率」如何影響溢洪道氣蝕防治的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Air supply and phase fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cavitation mitigation in spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"供氣可緩和氣泡潰滅附近的局部壓力衝擊，但入口總氣量不等於近壁保護濃度。水氣體積比需以相同壓力溫度定義，並區分氣水比與混合物空隙率；氣泡滑移與沿程脫氣使兩者的空間分布更複雜。 驗證時應同步量測供氣管流量與底部含氣剖面並標記壓力溫度，並辨識以下失效情境：總供氣量正常但氣泡浮離底部仍可能缺乏保護。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「摻氣量與相分率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Air supply can cushion local collapse pressures, but total supplied air is not near-wall protective concentration. Use consistent pressure and temperature and distinguish air-to-water volume ratio from mixture void fraction. Bubble slip and downstream detrainment complicate the spatial distribution further. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure vent supply and near-bed air profiles together with pressure and temperature. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Normal total supply can coexist with poor protection when bubbles leave the bed. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Air supply and phase fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Qa=6 m3/s andQw=54 m3/s at common conditions; bulkVoidFraction=6/(6+54)=0.10。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Qa=6 m3/s andQw=54 m3/s at common conditions; bulkVoidFraction=6/(6+54)=0.10.","failure":"常見誤解：「總供氣量足夠就保證每個壁面都有足夠含氣」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate total air supply guarantees adequate aeration at every wall\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「摻氣量與相分率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Air supply and phase fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-17-k1","title":"摻氣量與相分率","titleEn":"Air supply and phase fraction","text":"供氣可緩和氣泡潰滅附近的局部壓力衝擊，但入口總氣量不等於近壁保護濃度。水氣體積比需以相同壓力溫度定義，並區分氣水比與混合物空隙率；氣泡滑移與沿程脫氣使兩者的空間分布更複雜。","textEn":"Air supply can cushion local collapse pressures, but total supplied air is not near-wall protective concentration. Use consistent pressure and temperature and distinguish air-to-water volume ratio from mixture void fraction.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總供氣量足夠就保證每個壁面都有足夠含氣 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate total air supply guarantees adequate aeration at every wall Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「摻氣量與相分率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Air supply and phase fraction\" is correct?","options":["總供氣量足夠就保證每個壁面都有足夠含氣","空腔越負壓就表示摻氣保護一定越好","供氣可緩和氣泡潰滅附近的局部壓力衝擊，但入口總氣量不等於近壁保護濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate total air supply guarantees adequate aeration at every wall","Stronger cavity suction always means better aeration protection","Air supply can cushion local collapse pressures, but total supplied air is not near-wall protective concentration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"供氣可緩和氣泡潰滅附近的局部壓力衝擊，但入口總氣量不等於近壁保護濃度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Air supply can cushion local collapse pressures, but total supplied air is not near-wall protective concentration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b249-v15-18","title":"摻氣量與相分率：定量估算","titleEn":"Air supply and phase fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「摻氣量與相分率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Air supply and phase fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Qa=6 m3/s andQw=54 m3/s at common conditions; bulkVoidFraction=6/(6+54)=0.10。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Qa=6 m3/s andQw=54 m3/s at common conditions; bulkVoidFraction=6/(6+54)=0.10. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測供氣管流量與底部含氣剖面並標記壓力溫度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure vent supply and near-bed air profiles together with pressure and temperature.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Qa=6 m3/s andQw=54 m3/s at common conditions; bulkVoidFraction=6/(6+54)=0.10。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Qa=6 m3/s andQw=54 m3/s at common conditions; bulkVoidFraction=6/(6+54)=0.10. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「摻氣量與相分率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Air supply and phase fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Qa=6 m3/s andQw=54 m3/s at common conditions; bulkVoidFraction=6/(6+54)=0.10。","一次損傷體積可直接預報未來每年的固定損失","所有運轉一小時造成的氣蝕損傷必定相同"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Qa=6 m3/s andQw=54 m3/s at common conditions; bulkVoidFraction=6/(6+54)=0.10.","One damage-volume survey predicts a fixed annual future loss","Every operating hour necessarily causes the same cavitation damage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Qa=6 m3/s andQw=54 m3/s at common conditions; bulkVoidFraction=6/(6+54)=0.10。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Qa=6 m3/s andQw=54 m3/s at common conditions; bulkVoidFraction=6/(6+54)=0.10. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b249-v15-19","title":"摻氣量與相分率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Air supply and phase fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「摻氣量與相分率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Air supply and phase fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測供氣管流量與底部含氣剖面並標記壓力溫度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「總供氣量正常但氣泡浮離底部仍可能缺乏保護」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure vent supply and near-bed air profiles together with pressure and temperature. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Normal total supply can coexist with poor protection when bubbles leave the bed. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步量測供氣管流量與底部含氣剖面並標記壓力溫度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對總供氣量正常但氣泡浮離底部仍可能缺乏保護，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure vent supply and near-bed air profiles together with pressure and temperature. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Normal total supply can coexist with poor protection when bubbles leave the bed. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：總供氣量正常但氣泡浮離底部仍可能缺乏保護。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Normal total supply can coexist with poor protection when bubbles leave the bed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測供氣管流量與底部含氣剖面並標記壓力溫度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「總供氣量正常但氣泡浮離底部仍可能缺乏保護」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure vent supply and near-bed air profiles together with pressure and temperature. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Normal total supply can coexist with poor protection when bubbles leave the bed. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步量測供氣管流量與底部含氣剖面並標記壓力溫度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對總供氣量正常但氣泡浮離底部仍可能缺乏保護，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure vent supply and near-bed air profiles together with pressure and temperature. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Normal total supply can coexist with poor protection when bubbles leave the bed. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「摻氣量與相分率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Air supply and phase fraction\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","同步量測供氣管流量與底部含氣剖面並標記壓力溫度。","氣蝕指標數值可直接換算成混凝土磨損速率"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure vent supply and near-bed air profiles together with pressure and temperature.","The cavitation index directly converts into a concrete damage rate"],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步量測供氣管流量與底部含氣剖面並標記壓力溫度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure vent supply and near-bed air profiles together with pressure and temperature. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b249-v15-20","title":"摻氣量與相分率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Air supply and phase fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「摻氣量與相分率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Air supply and phase fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"總供氣量正常但氣泡浮離底部仍可能缺乏保護。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測供氣管流量與底部含氣剖面並標記壓力溫度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Normal total supply can coexist with poor protection when bubbles leave the bed. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure vent supply and near-bed air profiles together with pressure and temperature. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總供氣量足夠就保證每個壁面都有足夠含氣」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate total air supply guarantees adequate aeration at every wall\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"總供氣量正常但氣泡浮離底部仍可能缺乏保護。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測供氣管流量與底部含氣剖面並標記壓力溫度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Normal total supply can coexist with poor protection when bubbles leave the bed. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure vent supply and near-bed air profiles together with pressure and temperature. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「摻氣量與相分率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Air supply and phase fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","空腔越負壓就表示摻氣保護一定越好","總供氣量正常但氣泡浮離底部仍可能缺乏保護。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Stronger cavity suction always means better aeration protection","Normal total supply can coexist with poor protection when bubbles leave the bed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"總供氣量正常但氣泡浮離底部仍可能缺乏保護。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Normal total supply can coexist with poor protection when bubbles leave the bed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b249-v15-21","title":"通氣管損失與負壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Vent losses and suction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「通氣管損失與負壓」如何影響溢洪道氣蝕防治的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Vent losses and suction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cavitation mitigation in spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"摻氣槽形成的空腔需透過通氣管補氣，管路阻力會降低空腔壓力並影響射流軌跡。低馬赫數近似可用局部損失估壓差；若壓差大或接近可壓縮限制，必須改用適當氣體流模型，不可直接照搬不可壓縮公式。 驗證時應量測通氣口與空腔壓差並檢查網罩和轉彎阻力，並辨識以下失效情境：通氣入口堵塞可降低供氣並加深空腔負壓。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「通氣管損失與負壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Aerator cavities draw air through ducts whose resistance changes cavity pressure and jet shape. At low Mach number, a local-loss relation estimates pressure drop. Large pressure differences or compressibility limits require a gas-flow model instead of unconditional use of an incompressible expression. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure inlet-to-cavity pressure drop and inspect screens and bends. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A blocked vent inlet reduces supply and deepens cavity suction. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Vent losses and suction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Low-Mach air: rhoAir=1.2 kg/m3; lossK=3; airV=20 m/s; pressureLoss=3*0.5*1.2*20**2=720 Pa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Low-Mach air: rhoAir=1.2 kg/m3; lossK=3; airV=20 m/s; pressureLoss=3*0.5*1.2*20**2=720 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「空腔越負壓就表示摻氣保護一定越好」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stronger cavity suction always means better aeration protection\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「通氣管損失與負壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Vent losses and suction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-21-k1","title":"通氣管損失與負壓","titleEn":"Vent losses and suction","text":"摻氣槽形成的空腔需透過通氣管補氣，管路阻力會降低空腔壓力並影響射流軌跡。低馬赫數近似可用局部損失估壓差；若壓差大或接近可壓縮限制，必須改用適當氣體流模型，不可直接照搬不可壓縮公式。","textEn":"Aerator cavities draw air through ducts whose resistance changes cavity pressure and jet shape. At low Mach number, a local-loss relation estimates pressure drop.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：空腔越負壓就表示摻氣保護一定越好 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stronger cavity suction always means better aeration protection Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通氣管損失與負壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Vent losses and suction\" is correct?","options":["摻氣槽形成的空腔需透過通氣管補氣，管路阻力會降低空腔壓力並影響射流軌跡。","空腔越負壓就表示摻氣保護一定越好","只要有摻氣坎就不可能發生空腔淹沒"],"optionsEn":["Aerator cavities draw air through ducts whose resistance changes cavity pressure and jet shape.","Stronger cavity suction always means better aeration protection","The presence of an aerator ramp makes cavity drowning impossible"],"answer":0,"explanation":"摻氣槽形成的空腔需透過通氣管補氣，管路阻力會降低空腔壓力並影響射流軌跡。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Aerator cavities draw air through ducts whose resistance changes cavity pressure and jet shape. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b249-v15-22","title":"通氣管損失與負壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Vent losses and suction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「通氣管損失與負壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Vent losses and suction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Low-Mach air: rhoAir=1.2 kg/m3; lossK=3; airV=20 m/s; pressureLoss=3*0.5*1.2*20**2=720 Pa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Low-Mach air: rhoAir=1.2 kg/m3; lossK=3; airV=20 m/s; pressureLoss=3*0.5*1.2*20**2=720 Pa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測通氣口與空腔壓差並檢查網罩和轉彎阻力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure inlet-to-cavity pressure drop and inspect screens and bends.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Low-Mach air: rhoAir=1.2 kg/m3; lossK=3; airV=20 m/s; pressureLoss=3*0.5*1.2*20**2=720 Pa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Low-Mach air: rhoAir=1.2 kg/m3; lossK=3; airV=20 m/s; pressureLoss=3*0.5*1.2*20**2=720 Pa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通氣管損失與負壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Vent losses and suction\", which statement holds?","options":["一個拉拔試點合格就證明整片修補完全黏結","原創教學假設：Low-Mach air: rhoAir=1.2 kg/m3; lossK=3; airV=20 m/s; pressureLoss=3*0.5*1.2*20**2=720 Pa。","表壓負值就表示液體一定已達蒸氣壓"],"optionsEn":["One passing pull-off test proves complete bond over the entire repair","Original teaching assumptions: Low-Mach air: rhoAir=1.2 kg/m3; lossK=3; airV=20 m/s; pressureLoss=3*0.5*1.2*20**2=720 Pa.","Any negative gauge pressure proves that liquid has reached vapor pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Low-Mach air: rhoAir=1.2 kg/m3; lossK=3; airV=20 m/s; pressureLoss=3*0.5*1.2*20**2=720 Pa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Low-Mach air: rhoAir=1.2 kg/m3; lossK=3; airV=20 m/s; pressureLoss=3*0.5*1.2*20**2=720 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b249-v15-23","title":"通氣管損失與負壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Vent losses and suction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「通氣管損失與負壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Vent losses and suction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測通氣口與空腔壓差並檢查網罩和轉彎阻力。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「通氣入口堵塞可降低供氣並加深空腔負壓」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure inlet-to-cavity pressure drop and inspect screens and bends. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A blocked vent inlet reduces supply and deepens cavity suction. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以量測通氣口與空腔壓差並檢查網罩和轉彎阻力作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對通氣入口堵塞可降低供氣並加深空腔負壓，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure inlet-to-cavity pressure drop and inspect screens and bends. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A blocked vent inlet reduces supply and deepens cavity suction. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：通氣入口堵塞可降低供氣並加深空腔負壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A blocked vent inlet reduces supply and deepens cavity suction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測通氣口與空腔壓差並檢查網罩和轉彎阻力。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「通氣入口堵塞可降低供氣並加深空腔負壓」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure inlet-to-cavity pressure drop and inspect screens and bends. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A blocked vent inlet reduces supply and deepens cavity suction. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以量測通氣口與空腔壓差並檢查網罩和轉彎阻力作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對通氣入口堵塞可降低供氣並加深空腔負壓，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure inlet-to-cavity pressure drop and inspect screens and bends. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A blocked vent inlet reduces supply and deepens cavity suction. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通氣管損失與負壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Vent losses and suction\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","相同錯台高度不論方向都有相同氣蝕影響","量測通氣口與空腔壓差並檢查網罩和轉彎阻力。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Equal offset heights have identical cavitation effects in every orientation","Measure inlet-to-cavity pressure drop and inspect screens and bends."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測通氣口與空腔壓差並檢查網罩和轉彎阻力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure inlet-to-cavity pressure drop and inspect screens and bends. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b249-v15-24","title":"通氣管損失與負壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Vent losses and suction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「通氣管損失與負壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Vent losses and suction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"通氣入口堵塞可降低供氣並加深空腔負壓。診斷時應採取以下查核：量測通氣口與空腔壓差並檢查網罩和轉彎阻力，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A blocked vent inlet reduces supply and deepens cavity suction. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure inlet-to-cavity pressure drop and inspect screens and bends. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「空腔越負壓就表示摻氣保護一定越好」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stronger cavity suction always means better aeration protection\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"通氣入口堵塞可降低供氣並加深空腔負壓。診斷時應採取以下查核：量測通氣口與空腔壓差並檢查網罩和轉彎阻力，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A blocked vent inlet reduces supply and deepens cavity suction. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure inlet-to-cavity pressure drop and inspect screens and bends. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通氣管損失與負壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Vent losses and suction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["通氣入口堵塞可降低供氣並加深空腔負壓。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要有摻氣坎就不可能發生空腔淹沒"],"optionsEn":["A blocked vent inlet reduces supply and deepens cavity suction.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","The presence of an aerator ramp makes cavity drowning impossible"],"answer":0,"explanation":"通氣入口堵塞可降低供氣並加深空腔負壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A blocked vent inlet reduces supply and deepens cavity suction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b249-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「拋離空腔與再附著」與「損傷盤點與體積」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Jet cavity and reattachment\" and \"Damage mapping and volume\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b249-v15-25","title":"拋離空腔與再附著：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Jet cavity and reattachment: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「拋離空腔與再附著」如何影響溢洪道氣蝕防治的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Jet cavity and reattachment” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cavitation mitigation in spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"摻氣坎讓水流暫時離開底板並在下方形成供氣空腔，水舌再附著位置影響近壁含氣與局部壓力。水平拋射簡式只估無阻力的中心線，不代表含氣分布；設計需同時檢查空腔是否淹沒與再附著後的保護長度。 驗證時應以影像量測空腔長度並檢查再附著後近壁含氣，並辨識以下失效情境：尾水或水深增大可能淹沒空腔並切斷補氣。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「拋離空腔與再附著」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An aerator ramp lifts flow from the floor and forms an air cavity. Reattachment affects near-wall air and pressure. A horizontal ballistic estimate gives only a drag-free centerline, not concentration. Check cavity drowning and protection downstream of reattachment as separate performance questions. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure cavity length optically and inspect near-wall air downstream of reattachment. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Higher water depth can drown the cavity and interrupt air supply. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Jet cavity and reattachment” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：HorizontalLaunchV=15 m/s; drop=0.20 m; flightTime=sqrt(2*0.20/9.81); range=15*sqrt(0.4/9.81)=3.02891 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: HorizontalLaunchV=15 m/s; drop=0.20 m; flightTime=sqrt(2*0.20/9.81); range=15*sqrt(0.4/9.81)=3.02891 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要有摻氣坎就不可能發生空腔淹沒」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The presence of an aerator ramp makes cavity drowning impossible\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「拋離空腔與再附著」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Jet cavity and reattachment”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-25-k1","title":"拋離空腔與再附著","titleEn":"Jet cavity and reattachment","text":"摻氣坎讓水流暫時離開底板並在下方形成供氣空腔，水舌再附著位置影響近壁含氣與局部壓力。水平拋射簡式只估無阻力的中心線，不代表含氣分布；設計需同時檢查空腔是否淹沒與再附著後的保護長度。","textEn":"An aerator ramp lifts flow from the floor and forms an air cavity. Reattachment affects near-wall air and pressure.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要有摻氣坎就不可能發生空腔淹沒 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The presence of an aerator ramp makes cavity drowning impossible Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「拋離空腔與再附著」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Jet cavity and reattachment\" is correct?","options":["只要有摻氣坎就不可能發生空腔淹沒","摻氣坎讓水流暫時離開底板並在下方形成供氣空腔，水舌再附著位置影響近壁含氣與局部壓力。","一次損傷體積可直接預報未來每年的固定損失"],"optionsEn":["The presence of an aerator ramp makes cavity drowning impossible","An aerator ramp lifts flow from the floor and forms an air cavity.","One damage-volume survey predicts a fixed annual future loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"摻氣坎讓水流暫時離開底板並在下方形成供氣空腔，水舌再附著位置影響近壁含氣與局部壓力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An aerator ramp lifts flow from the floor and forms an air cavity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b249-v15-26","title":"拋離空腔與再附著：定量估算","titleEn":"Jet cavity and reattachment: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「拋離空腔與再附著」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Jet cavity and reattachment” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：HorizontalLaunchV=15 m/s; drop=0.20 m; flightTime=sqrt(2*0.20/9.81); range=15*sqrt(0.4/9.81)=3.02891 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: HorizontalLaunchV=15 m/s; drop=0.20 m; flightTime=sqrt(2*0.20/9.81); range=15*sqrt(0.4/9.81)=3.02891 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以影像量測空腔長度並檢查再附著後近壁含氣。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure cavity length optically and inspect near-wall air downstream of reattachment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：HorizontalLaunchV=15 m/s; drop=0.20 m; flightTime=sqrt(2*0.20/9.81); range=15*sqrt(0.4/9.81)=3.02891 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HorizontalLaunchV=15 m/s; drop=0.20 m; flightTime=sqrt(2*0.20/9.81); range=15*sqrt(0.4/9.81)=3.02891 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「拋離空腔與再附著」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Jet cavity and reattachment\", which statement holds?","options":["所有運轉一小時造成的氣蝕損傷必定相同","氣蝕指標數值可直接換算成混凝土磨損速率","原創教學假設：HorizontalLaunchV=15 m/s; drop=0.20 m; flightTime=sqrt(2*0.20/9.81); range=15*sqrt(0.4/9.81)=3.02891 m。"],"optionsEn":["Every operating hour necessarily causes the same cavitation damage","The cavitation index directly converts into a concrete damage rate","Original teaching assumptions: HorizontalLaunchV=15 m/s; drop=0.20 m; flightTime=sqrt(2*0.20/9.81); range=15*sqrt(0.4/9.81)=3.02891 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：HorizontalLaunchV=15 m/s; drop=0.20 m; flightTime=sqrt(2*0.20/9.81); range=15*sqrt(0.4/9.81)=3.02891 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HorizontalLaunchV=15 m/s; drop=0.20 m; flightTime=sqrt(2*0.20/9.81); range=15*sqrt(0.4/9.81)=3.02891 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b249-v15-27","title":"拋離空腔與再附著：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Jet cavity and reattachment: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「拋離空腔與再附著」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Jet cavity and reattachment” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以影像量測空腔長度並檢查再附著後近壁含氣。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「尾水或水深增大可能淹沒空腔並切斷補氣」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure cavity length optically and inspect near-wall air downstream of reattachment. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Higher water depth can drown the cavity and interrupt air supply. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以影像量測空腔長度並檢查再附著後近壁含氣作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對尾水或水深增大可能淹沒空腔並切斷補氣，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure cavity length optically and inspect near-wall air downstream of reattachment. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Higher water depth can drown the cavity and interrupt air supply. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：尾水或水深增大可能淹沒空腔並切斷補氣。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Higher water depth can drown the cavity and interrupt air supply. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以影像量測空腔長度並檢查再附著後近壁含氣。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「尾水或水深增大可能淹沒空腔並切斷補氣」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure cavity length optically and inspect near-wall air downstream of reattachment. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Higher water depth can drown the cavity and interrupt air supply. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以影像量測空腔長度並檢查再附著後近壁含氣作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對尾水或水深增大可能淹沒空腔並切斷補氣，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure cavity length optically and inspect near-wall air downstream of reattachment. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Higher water depth can drown the cavity and interrupt air supply. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「拋離空腔與再附著」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Jet cavity and reattachment\"?","options":["以影像量測空腔長度並檢查再附著後近壁含氣。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","平均壓力高於蒸氣壓就排除所有瞬間氣蝕"],"optionsEn":["Measure cavity length optically and inspect near-wall air downstream of reattachment.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Mean pressure above vapor pressure excludes every transient cavitation event"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以影像量測空腔長度並檢查再附著後近壁含氣。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure cavity length optically and inspect near-wall air downstream of reattachment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b249-v15-28","title":"拋離空腔與再附著：失效診斷","titleEn":"Jet cavity and reattachment: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「拋離空腔與再附著」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Jet cavity and reattachment” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"尾水或水深增大可能淹沒空腔並切斷補氣。診斷時應採取以下查核：以影像量測空腔長度並檢查再附著後近壁含氣，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Higher water depth can drown the cavity and interrupt air supply. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure cavity length optically and inspect near-wall air downstream of reattachment. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要有摻氣坎就不可能發生空腔淹沒」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The presence of an aerator ramp makes cavity drowning impossible\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"尾水或水深增大可能淹沒空腔並切斷補氣。診斷時應採取以下查核：以影像量測空腔長度並檢查再附著後近壁含氣，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Higher water depth can drown the cavity and interrupt air supply. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure cavity length optically and inspect near-wall air downstream of reattachment. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「拋離空腔與再附著」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Jet cavity and reattachment\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","尾水或水深增大可能淹沒空腔並切斷補氣。","一次損傷體積可直接預報未來每年的固定損失"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Higher water depth can drown the cavity and interrupt air supply.","One damage-volume survey predicts a fixed annual future loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"尾水或水深增大可能淹沒空腔並切斷補氣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Higher water depth can drown the cavity and interrupt air supply. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b249-v15-29","title":"損傷盤點與體積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Damage mapping and volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「損傷盤點與體積」如何影響溢洪道氣蝕防治的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Damage mapping and volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cavitation mitigation in spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"氣蝕損傷可能由局部凹坑成長並改變後續流場，修補前需建立可重複的地形基準。面積乘平均深度只是體積盤點，不能把它當作未來線性損傷率；磨耗、化學侵蝕與鋼筋剝露需分別辨認並追溯操作歷程。 驗證時應用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄，並辨識以下失效情境：以單次平均損傷量線性外推可能漏掉幾何惡化的加速效應。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「損傷盤點與體積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cavitation pits can grow and alter subsequent flow. Establish a repeatable surface datum before repair. Area times mean depth estimates lost volume, not a linear future damage rate. Distinguish abrasion, chemical deterioration and exposed reinforcement and relate each to the operating history. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Linear extrapolation from one survey misses acceleration caused by worsening geometry. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Damage mapping and volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：damagedArea=12 m2; meanLossDepth=0.025 m; lostVolume=12*0.025=0.30 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: damagedArea=12 m2; meanLossDepth=0.025 m; lostVolume=12*0.025=0.30 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「一次損傷體積可直接預報未來每年的固定損失」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One damage-volume survey predicts a fixed annual future loss\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「損傷盤點與體積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Damage mapping and volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-29-k1","title":"損傷盤點與體積","titleEn":"Damage mapping and volume","text":"氣蝕損傷可能由局部凹坑成長並改變後續流場，修補前需建立可重複的地形基準。面積乘平均深度只是體積盤點，不能把它當作未來線性損傷率；磨耗、化學侵蝕與鋼筋剝露需分別辨認並追溯操作歷程。","textEn":"Cavitation pits can grow and alter subsequent flow. Establish a repeatable surface datum before repair.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：一次損傷體積可直接預報未來每年的固定損失 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One damage-volume survey predicts a fixed annual future loss Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「損傷盤點與體積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Damage mapping and volume\" is correct?","options":["一次損傷體積可直接預報未來每年的固定損失","一個拉拔試點合格就證明整片修補完全黏結","氣蝕損傷可能由局部凹坑成長並改變後續流場，修補前需建立可重複的地形基準。"],"optionsEn":["One damage-volume survey predicts a fixed annual future loss","One passing pull-off test proves complete bond over the entire repair","Cavitation pits can grow and alter subsequent flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"氣蝕損傷可能由局部凹坑成長並改變後續流場，修補前需建立可重複的地形基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cavitation pits can grow and alter subsequent flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b249-v15-30","title":"損傷盤點與體積：定量估算","titleEn":"Damage mapping and volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「損傷盤點與體積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Damage mapping and volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：damagedArea=12 m2; meanLossDepth=0.025 m; lostVolume=12*0.025=0.30 m3。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: damagedArea=12 m2; meanLossDepth=0.025 m; lostVolume=12*0.025=0.30 m3. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：damagedArea=12 m2; meanLossDepth=0.025 m; lostVolume=12*0.025=0.30 m3。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: damagedArea=12 m2; meanLossDepth=0.025 m; lostVolume=12*0.025=0.30 m3. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「損傷盤點與體積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Damage mapping and volume\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：damagedArea=12 m2; meanLossDepth=0.025 m; lostVolume=12*0.025=0.30 m3。","表壓負值就表示液體一定已達蒸氣壓","相同錯台高度不論方向都有相同氣蝕影響"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: damagedArea=12 m2; meanLossDepth=0.025 m; lostVolume=12*0.025=0.30 m3.","Any negative gauge pressure proves that liquid has reached vapor pressure","Equal offset heights have identical cavitation effects in every orientation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：damagedArea=12 m2; meanLossDepth=0.025 m; lostVolume=12*0.025=0.30 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: damagedArea=12 m2; meanLossDepth=0.025 m; lostVolume=12*0.025=0.30 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b249-v15-31","title":"損傷盤點與體積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Damage mapping and volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「損傷盤點與體積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Damage mapping and volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「以單次平均損傷量線性外推可能漏掉幾何惡化的加速效應」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Linear extrapolation from one survey misses acceleration caused by worsening geometry. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對以單次平均損傷量線性外推可能漏掉幾何惡化的加速效應，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Linear extrapolation from one survey misses acceleration caused by worsening geometry. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：以單次平均損傷量線性外推可能漏掉幾何惡化的加速效應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Linear extrapolation from one survey misses acceleration caused by worsening geometry. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「以單次平均損傷量線性外推可能漏掉幾何惡化的加速效應」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Linear extrapolation from one survey misses acceleration caused by worsening geometry. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對以單次平均損傷量線性外推可能漏掉幾何惡化的加速效應，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Linear extrapolation from one survey misses acceleration caused by worsening geometry. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「損傷盤點與體積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Damage mapping and volume\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄。","總供氣量足夠就保證每個壁面都有足夠含氣"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records.","Adequate total air supply guarantees adequate aeration at every wall"],"answer":1,"explanation":"用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b249-v15-32","title":"損傷盤點與體積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Damage mapping and volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「損傷盤點與體積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Damage mapping and volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以單次平均損傷量線性外推可能漏掉幾何惡化的加速效應。診斷時應採取以下查核：用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Linear extrapolation from one survey misses acceleration caused by worsening geometry. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「一次損傷體積可直接預報未來每年的固定損失」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One damage-volume survey predicts a fixed annual future loss\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以單次平均損傷量線性外推可能漏掉幾何惡化的加速效應。診斷時應採取以下查核：用重複三維掃描比較凹坑位置體積並保留運轉流量紀錄，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Linear extrapolation from one survey misses acceleration caused by worsening geometry. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare repeated three-dimensional pit maps and volumes against operating discharge records. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「損傷盤點與體積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Damage mapping and volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","一個拉拔試點合格就證明整片修補完全黏結","以單次平均損傷量線性外推可能漏掉幾何惡化的加速效應。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","One passing pull-off test proves complete bond over the entire repair","Linear extrapolation from one survey misses acceleration caused by worsening geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以單次平均損傷量線性外推可能漏掉幾何惡化的加速效應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Linear extrapolation from one survey misses acceleration caused by worsening geometry. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b249-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「修補黏結與平整」與「運轉曝露與追蹤」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Repair bond and surface continuity\" and \"Operating exposure and follow-up\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b249-v15-33","title":"修補黏結與平整：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Repair bond and surface continuity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「修補黏結與平整」如何影響溢洪道氣蝕防治的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Repair bond and surface continuity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cavitation mitigation in spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"修補材料需與基材共同承受水力脈壓及溫度變形，表面平順與黏結完整同樣重要。拉拔試驗只檢查局部黏結樣本，不能證明整片無空鼓；施工記錄應包含基面處理、養護與沿流接縫輪廓，避免修補本身形成新缺陷。 驗證時應結合拉拔位置圖敲測或適用非破壞檢查與表面剖面，並辨識以下失效情境：局部拉拔合格仍可能存在未取樣的空鼓帶。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「修補黏結與平整」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Repairs must transfer hydraulic pulses and thermal deformation to the substrate. Smoothness and bond continuity both matter. Pull-off tests sample local adhesion and cannot prove an entire patch void-free; document preparation, curing and flowwise joint profiles so the repair does not create another initiating defect. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Combine mapped pull-off locations, suitable void detection and surface profiles. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Passing local pull-off tests can coexist with an unsampled debonded strip. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Repair bond and surface continuity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：PullOffLoad=9 kN; testArea=0.003 m2; nominalBondStress=9/0.003/1000=3 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: PullOffLoad=9 kN; testArea=0.003 m2; nominalBondStress=9/0.003/1000=3 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「一個拉拔試點合格就證明整片修補完全黏結」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One passing pull-off test proves complete bond over the entire repair\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「修補黏結與平整」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Repair bond and surface continuity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-33-k1","title":"修補黏結與平整","titleEn":"Repair bond and surface continuity","text":"修補材料需與基材共同承受水力脈壓及溫度變形，表面平順與黏結完整同樣重要。拉拔試驗只檢查局部黏結樣本，不能證明整片無空鼓；施工記錄應包含基面處理、養護與沿流接縫輪廓，避免修補本身形成新缺陷。","textEn":"Repairs must transfer hydraulic pulses and thermal deformation to the substrate. Smoothness and bond continuity both matter.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：一個拉拔試點合格就證明整片修補完全黏結 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One passing pull-off test proves complete bond over the entire repair Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「修補黏結與平整」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Repair bond and surface continuity\" is correct?","options":["修補材料需與基材共同承受水力脈壓及溫度變形，表面平順與黏結完整同樣重要。","一個拉拔試點合格就證明整片修補完全黏結","所有運轉一小時造成的氣蝕損傷必定相同"],"optionsEn":["Repairs must transfer hydraulic pulses and thermal deformation to the substrate.","One passing pull-off test proves complete bond over the entire repair","Every operating hour necessarily causes the same cavitation damage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"修補材料需與基材共同承受水力脈壓及溫度變形，表面平順與黏結完整同樣重要。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Repairs must transfer hydraulic pulses and thermal deformation to the substrate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b249-v15-34","title":"修補黏結與平整：定量估算","titleEn":"Repair bond and surface continuity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「修補黏結與平整」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Repair bond and surface continuity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：PullOffLoad=9 kN; testArea=0.003 m2; nominalBondStress=9/0.003/1000=3 MPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: PullOffLoad=9 kN; testArea=0.003 m2; nominalBondStress=9/0.003/1000=3 MPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：結合拉拔位置圖敲測或適用非破壞檢查與表面剖面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Combine mapped pull-off locations, suitable void detection and surface profiles.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：PullOffLoad=9 kN; testArea=0.003 m2; nominalBondStress=9/0.003/1000=3 MPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: PullOffLoad=9 kN; testArea=0.003 m2; nominalBondStress=9/0.003/1000=3 MPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「修補黏結與平整」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Repair bond and surface continuity\", which statement holds?","options":["氣蝕指標數值可直接換算成混凝土磨損速率","原創教學假設：PullOffLoad=9 kN; testArea=0.003 m2; nominalBondStress=9/0.003/1000=3 MPa。","平均壓力高於蒸氣壓就排除所有瞬間氣蝕"],"optionsEn":["The cavitation index directly converts into a concrete damage rate","Original teaching assumptions: PullOffLoad=9 kN; testArea=0.003 m2; nominalBondStress=9/0.003/1000=3 MPa.","Mean pressure above vapor pressure excludes every transient cavitation event"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：PullOffLoad=9 kN; testArea=0.003 m2; nominalBondStress=9/0.003/1000=3 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: PullOffLoad=9 kN; testArea=0.003 m2; nominalBondStress=9/0.003/1000=3 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b249-v15-35","title":"修補黏結與平整：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Repair bond and surface continuity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「修補黏結與平整」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Repair bond and surface continuity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"結合拉拔位置圖敲測或適用非破壞檢查與表面剖面。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「局部拉拔合格仍可能存在未取樣的空鼓帶」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Combine mapped pull-off locations, suitable void detection and surface profiles. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Passing local pull-off tests can coexist with an unsampled debonded strip. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以結合拉拔位置圖敲測或適用非破壞檢查與表面剖面作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對局部拉拔合格仍可能存在未取樣的空鼓帶，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Combine mapped pull-off locations, suitable void detection and surface profiles. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Passing local pull-off tests can coexist with an unsampled debonded strip. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：局部拉拔合格仍可能存在未取樣的空鼓帶。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Passing local pull-off tests can coexist with an unsampled debonded strip. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"結合拉拔位置圖敲測或適用非破壞檢查與表面剖面。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「局部拉拔合格仍可能存在未取樣的空鼓帶」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Combine mapped pull-off locations, suitable void detection and surface profiles. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Passing local pull-off tests can coexist with an unsampled debonded strip. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以結合拉拔位置圖敲測或適用非破壞檢查與表面剖面作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對局部拉拔合格仍可能存在未取樣的空鼓帶，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Combine mapped pull-off locations, suitable void detection and surface profiles. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Passing local pull-off tests can coexist with an unsampled debonded strip. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「修補黏結與平整」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Repair bond and surface continuity\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","空腔越負壓就表示摻氣保護一定越好","結合拉拔位置圖敲測或適用非破壞檢查與表面剖面。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Stronger cavity suction always means better aeration protection","Combine mapped pull-off locations, suitable void detection and surface profiles."],"answer":2,"explanation":"結合拉拔位置圖敲測或適用非破壞檢查與表面剖面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Combine mapped pull-off locations, suitable void detection and surface profiles. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b249-v15-36","title":"修補黏結與平整：失效診斷","titleEn":"Repair bond and surface continuity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「修補黏結與平整」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Repair bond and surface continuity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部拉拔合格仍可能存在未取樣的空鼓帶。診斷時應採取以下查核：結合拉拔位置圖敲測或適用非破壞檢查與表面剖面，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Passing local pull-off tests can coexist with an unsampled debonded strip. Diagnose it by the following check: Combine mapped pull-off locations, suitable void detection and surface profiles. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「一個拉拔試點合格就證明整片修補完全黏結」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One passing pull-off test proves complete bond over the entire repair\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部拉拔合格仍可能存在未取樣的空鼓帶。診斷時應採取以下查核：結合拉拔位置圖敲測或適用非破壞檢查與表面剖面，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Passing local pull-off tests can coexist with an unsampled debonded strip. Diagnose it by the following check: Combine mapped pull-off locations, suitable void detection and surface profiles. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「修補黏結與平整」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Repair bond and surface continuity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["局部拉拔合格仍可能存在未取樣的空鼓帶。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","所有運轉一小時造成的氣蝕損傷必定相同"],"optionsEn":["Passing local pull-off tests can coexist with an unsampled debonded strip.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Every operating hour necessarily causes the same cavitation damage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部拉拔合格仍可能存在未取樣的空鼓帶。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Passing local pull-off tests can coexist with an unsampled debonded strip. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b249-v15-37","title":"運轉曝露與追蹤：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Operating exposure and follow-up: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「運轉曝露與追蹤」如何影響溢洪道氣蝕防治的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Operating exposure and follow-up” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cavitation mitigation in spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"氣蝕損傷與高風險工況的持續時間有關，但不同流速與壓力不能以相同小時數直接等價。曝露時數可建立追蹤帳，仍須按流量、水位、含氣與缺陷狀態分組；修補後對照試驗應保持工況可比，才能辨識改善。 驗證時應按流量水位與含氣狀態分組比較修補前後檢測，並辨識以下失效情境：只比較總時數會掩蓋高速度短時工況的不同作用。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「運轉曝露與追蹤」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Damage depends on exposure to adverse conditions, but hours at different pressures and velocities are not equivalent. An exposure ledger supports tracking only when grouped by discharge, stage, aeration and surface condition. Postrepair comparisons need matched states before attributing changes to the repair. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Group inspections by discharge, stage and aeration when comparing before and after repair. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Comparing total hours alone hides the different effects of brief high-speed operation. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Operating exposure and follow-up” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Three identified operating intervals=2.5,1.0,3.5 h; totalRecordedExposure=2.5+1.0+3.5=7 h; no linear damage law。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Three identified operating intervals=2.5,1.0,3.5 h; totalRecordedExposure=2.5+1.0+3.5=7 h; no linear damage law.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有運轉一小時造成的氣蝕損傷必定相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every operating hour necessarily causes the same cavitation damage\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「運轉曝露與追蹤」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Operating exposure and follow-up”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-37-k1","title":"運轉曝露與追蹤","titleEn":"Operating exposure and follow-up","text":"氣蝕損傷與高風險工況的持續時間有關，但不同流速與壓力不能以相同小時數直接等價。曝露時數可建立追蹤帳，仍須按流量、水位、含氣與缺陷狀態分組；修補後對照試驗應保持工況可比，才能辨識改善。","textEn":"Damage depends on exposure to adverse conditions, but hours at different pressures and velocities are not equivalent. An exposure ledger supports tracking only when grouped by discharge, stage, aeration and surface condition.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有運轉一小時造成的氣蝕損傷必定相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every operating hour necessarily causes the same cavitation damage Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「運轉曝露與追蹤」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Operating exposure and follow-up\" is correct?","options":["所有運轉一小時造成的氣蝕損傷必定相同","氣蝕損傷與高風險工況的持續時間有關，但不同流速與壓力不能以相同小時數直接等價。","表壓負值就表示液體一定已達蒸氣壓"],"optionsEn":["Every operating hour necessarily causes the same cavitation damage","Damage depends on exposure to adverse conditions, but hours at different pressures and velocities are not equivalent.","Any negative gauge pressure proves that liquid has reached vapor pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"氣蝕損傷與高風險工況的持續時間有關，但不同流速與壓力不能以相同小時數直接等價。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Damage depends on exposure to adverse conditions, but hours at different pressures and velocities are not equivalent. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b249-v15-38","title":"運轉曝露與追蹤：定量估算","titleEn":"Operating exposure and follow-up: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「運轉曝露與追蹤」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Operating exposure and follow-up” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Three identified operating intervals=2.5,1.0,3.5 h; totalRecordedExposure=2.5+1.0+3.5=7 h; no linear damage law。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Three identified operating intervals=2.5,1.0,3.5 h; totalRecordedExposure=2.5+1.0+3.5=7 h; no linear damage law. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按流量水位與含氣狀態分組比較修補前後檢測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Group inspections by discharge, stage and aeration when comparing before and after repair.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Three identified operating intervals=2.5,1.0,3.5 h; totalRecordedExposure=2.5+1.0+3.5=7 h; no linear damage law。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Three identified operating intervals=2.5,1.0,3.5 h; totalRecordedExposure=2.5+1.0+3.5=7 h; no linear damage law. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「運轉曝露與追蹤」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Operating exposure and follow-up\", which statement holds?","options":["相同錯台高度不論方向都有相同氣蝕影響","總供氣量足夠就保證每個壁面都有足夠含氣","原創教學假設：Three identified operating intervals=2.5,1.0,3.5 h; totalRecordedExposure=2.5+1.0+3.5=7 h; no linear damage law。"],"optionsEn":["Equal offset heights have identical cavitation effects in every orientation","Adequate total air supply guarantees adequate aeration at every wall","Original teaching assumptions: Three identified operating intervals=2.5,1.0,3.5 h; totalRecordedExposure=2.5+1.0+3.5=7 h; no linear damage law."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Three identified operating intervals=2.5,1.0,3.5 h; totalRecordedExposure=2.5+1.0+3.5=7 h; no linear damage law。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Three identified operating intervals=2.5,1.0,3.5 h; totalRecordedExposure=2.5+1.0+3.5=7 h; no linear damage law. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b249-v15-39","title":"運轉曝露與追蹤：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Operating exposure and follow-up: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「運轉曝露與追蹤」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Operating exposure and follow-up” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按流量水位與含氣狀態分組比較修補前後檢測。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只比較總時數會掩蓋高速度短時工況的不同作用」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Group inspections by discharge, stage and aeration when comparing before and after repair. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Comparing total hours alone hides the different effects of brief high-speed operation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以按流量水位與含氣狀態分組比較修補前後檢測作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只比較總時數會掩蓋高速度短時工況的不同作用，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Group inspections by discharge, stage and aeration when comparing before and after repair. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Comparing total hours alone hides the different effects of brief high-speed operation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只比較總時數會掩蓋高速度短時工況的不同作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing total hours alone hides the different effects of brief high-speed operation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按流量水位與含氣狀態分組比較修補前後檢測。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只比較總時數會掩蓋高速度短時工況的不同作用」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Group inspections by discharge, stage and aeration when comparing before and after repair. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Comparing total hours alone hides the different effects of brief high-speed operation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以按流量水位與含氣狀態分組比較修補前後檢測作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只比較總時數會掩蓋高速度短時工況的不同作用，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Group inspections by discharge, stage and aeration when comparing before and after repair. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Comparing total hours alone hides the different effects of brief high-speed operation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「運轉曝露與追蹤」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Operating exposure and follow-up\"?","options":["按流量水位與含氣狀態分組比較修補前後檢測。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要有摻氣坎就不可能發生空腔淹沒"],"optionsEn":["Group inspections by discharge, stage and aeration when comparing before and after repair.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The presence of an aerator ramp makes cavity drowning impossible"],"answer":0,"explanation":"按流量水位與含氣狀態分組比較修補前後檢測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Group inspections by discharge, stage and aeration when comparing before and after repair. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b249-v15-40","title":"運轉曝露與追蹤：失效診斷","titleEn":"Operating exposure and follow-up: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b249-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「運轉曝露與追蹤」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Operating exposure and follow-up” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只比較總時數會掩蓋高速度短時工況的不同作用。診斷時應採取以下查核：按流量水位與含氣狀態分組比較修補前後檢測，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing total hours alone hides the different effects of brief high-speed operation. Diagnose it by the following check: Group inspections by discharge, stage and aeration when comparing before and after repair. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有運轉一小時造成的氣蝕損傷必定相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every operating hour necessarily causes the same cavitation damage\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b249-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只比較總時數會掩蓋高速度短時工況的不同作用。診斷時應採取以下查核：按流量水位與含氣狀態分組比較修補前後檢測，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Comparing total hours alone hides the different effects of brief high-speed operation. Diagnose it by the following check: Group inspections by discharge, stage and aeration when comparing before and after repair. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b249-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「運轉曝露與追蹤」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Operating exposure and follow-up\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只比較總時數會掩蓋高速度短時工況的不同作用。","表壓負值就表示液體一定已達蒸氣壓"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Comparing total hours alone hides the different effects of brief high-speed operation.","Any negative gauge pressure proves that liquid has reached vapor pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"只比較總時數會掩蓋高速度短時工況的不同作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing total hours alone hides the different effects of brief high-speed operation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-spillwaypro","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-research-catalog","v15s-glen-owner"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
